  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 955 PM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nThe long term period will be largely influenced by an upper level\nridge and subsequent sfc high over the southern Plains into the \nDeep South. As a result, the Tennessee Valley will remain in a NW\nflow pattern through mid week with a rising temperature trend. \nHigh temperatures are forecast to reach the low to mid 90s on \nMonday and will increase into the upper 90s by Tuesday. Heat \nproducts may be considered in future updates this weekend as heat \nindex temperatures are forecast to warm near or above 105 degrees.\nMid week, slight relief from heat is on the table as a frontal \nboundary drops southward from a potential low pressure system \nshifting into the northeast Appalachian region. However, \nconfidence is low in this at this time as it will depend on upper \nlevel trough placement/depth. Have continued with blended guidance\nat this time, which brings low chances (30% or less) of rainfall \nback to the area Wednesday into Thursday to account for the \npotential frontal boundary.",
